  "title": "Simon-conflict Task.",
  "description": "EEG recordings from 146 participants (98 individuals with Parkinson's disease and 48 controls) performing a Simon conflict task. Stimuli appeared on the left or right side of the screen, and participants responded with a left or right key according to stimulus color. Trials were spatially congruent or incongruent with the response hand. Data were collected alongside other cognitive tasks to study conflict processing and midfrontal activity in Parkinson's disease.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a 64-channel BrainVision cap during a Simon task. Participants pressed a left key for yellow or red stimuli and a right key for cyan or blue stimuli. Stimuli were presented on the left or right side of the screen, giving congruent and incongruent trials that were analyzed separately.",
